{"text": "ALDAMA IMMIGRATION COUNSEL PLLC -- INTAKE NOTES (atty-client privileged)\n\nConsult: Thurs 2/19/26, 10:30am, in person w/ Uzbek/Russian interpreter (Sevara, staff)\nAtty: B. Aldama        New matter #: 26-0188\nReferred by: cousin Otabek Nazarov (former client, file 23-0611)\n\nPC: Dilnoza Yusupova  (passport spells it \"YUSUPOVA DILNOZA BAKHTIYOROVNA\")\nDOB 14 Sept 1988, Samarkand. Uzbek citizen, ethnic Tajik. Sunni Muslim, not practicing.\nUzbekistan ppt FA2217409, exp 03/2029.\nA# 220-417-883 (from biometrics notice).  I-94 # 64418820733\nAdmitted JFK 08/03/2023 as B-2, stay authorized to 02/02/2024  -> out of status since Feb 2024 except for the pending asylum app.\nAddr: 7214 Frankford Ave, 2nd Fl rear, Philadelphia PA 19135\nCell 267-555-0148 (WhatsApp + Telegram same #, handle @dilnoza_writes).  Email d.yusupova88@inbox.example\nITIN 943-88-4417 (got it for the 2024 return)\n\nSpouse: Rustam Yusupov, DOB 3/9/1985, entered w/ her on same B-2. No A#.\nWorks for cash at Kensington Auto Upholstery (owner \"Mr. Lev\") -- NO work authorization.\nRustam: retail theft citation 2025, Bucks County, ARD completed; docket MJ-07104-NT-0000417-2025. Need certified disposition.\n\nKids:\n 1. Kamila, b. 22.11.2016 Tashkent, Uzbek ppt FA3380162, came w/ parents (rider on mom's I-589).\n    4th grade, Pennypack Creek Elementary. Asthma, albuterol inhaler.\n 2. Timur, b. June 6 2024, Philadelphia -> USC by birth. PA birth cert state file no. 136-24-0418872\n\nClaim (her words, summarized):\n - Wrote for the independent Telegram channel \"Zarafshon Ovozi\" about forced labor in the cotton harvest. She was the only reporter who covered the 2022 Jizzakh cotton story under her own name.\n - Detained two days by security services in June 2022; phone and laptop seized. Summoned twice more before they left.\n - her brother-in-law Jahongir (Jahongir Yusupov) is still in pretrial detention in Samarkand.\n - Affirmative Form I-589 filed pro se 01/18/2024 with help of a \"notario\", Lyudmila Korzun, paid $1,800 cash. Receipt no. ZNK2450041877.\n   Filed inside one year of entry so INA § 208(a)(2)(B) is fine. Korzun kept the originals - demand letter.\n - Interview notice: asylum office, Lyndhurst NJ? (she is not sure), 04/22/2026. Calendar it. 8 CFR § 208.7 clock running; EAD (c)(8) expires July 30 -> renew now, Form I-765.\n\nHealth: PTSD and insomnia, sees Maryam Jalali, LCSW at Tacony Family Wellness Collaborative every other week. Get a letter from Ms. Jalali. Dilnoza is 14 weeks pregnant (due mid-August).\n\nFee: Quoted $6,500 flat for asylum representation through interview + $1,200 for both EAD renewals. Paid $1,000 cash today, receipt #4471. Balance $500/mo starting 3/15.\n\nTO DO\n - FOIA (Form G-639) for her A-file and the I-94 history\n - Upload link sent: https://clients.aldama-immigration.example/upload/26-0188\n - Bring: both passports, Kamila's school records, Timur's birth cert, anything from Otabek who can corroborate the 2022 detention\n - Other atty on file will be Beatriz Aldama only. Interpreter for prep: Sevara Tursunova, 215.555.0107", "kind": "Text file", "detail": "451 words", "notes": [], "names": {"people": ["B. Aldama", "Dilnoza Yusupova", "Rustam Yusupov", "Kamila", "Timur", "Lyudmila Korzun", "Jahongir Yusupov", "Maryam Jalali", "Dilnoza", "Beatriz Aldama", "Sevara Tursunova"], "companies": ["ALDAMA IMMIGRATION COUNSEL PLLC", "Kensington Auto Upholstery", "Tacony Family Wellness Collaborative", "Aldama-immigration"]}, "chunks": 2, "chunkErrors": 0, "importMs": 0.8000000007450581, "modelMs": 38311.900000002235, "detectors": ["email", "url", "ip", "iban", "card", "card_exp", "cvv", "ssn", "bn_ca", "sin_ca", "ein", "phone", "dob", "age90", "date", "passport_dl", "routing", "credential", "device", "vin", "record", "account", "money", "street", "zip", "postal_ca", "places", "names"], "detections": [{"start": 0, "end": 31, "text": "ALDAMA IMMIGRATION COUNSEL PLLC", "kind": "company", "source": "short-form", "canoni